{"uuid":"EB73AD2A-7CDA-5F81-BE2E-B84130BDFB9B","name":"Mediterranean Turkey Bowls","serves":10,"duration":20,"cookingDuration":55,"defaultScale":1,"isPublicRecipe":false,"folderIDs":[],"ingredients":[{"uuid":"18CC3920-4BA4-5C42-A4B9-9C4BC56963D1","order":0,"ingredient":{"uuid":"4E7EEA1E-B644-55CB-B577-1B8855E1E2D4","name":"packages ground turkey (93/7), ~4.8 lbs total"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":4}},{"uuid":"D80CB595-6A87-5BD6-9E51-D657F794E995","order":1,"ingredient":{"uuid":"87AC7B3F-589B-5D71-988B-57AF6CA4E032","name":"dried oregano"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":2}},{"uuid":"ED0A82C3-7D06-5557-9740-827C53BC64F8","order":2,"ingredient":{"uuid":"59A146A9-50F6-5071-AAF3-EAA9B11A2D2D","name":"cloves garlic, minced"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":6}},{"uuid":"051680E1-1412-5116-98B4-712B25F5903B","order":3,"ingredient":{"uuid":"83689DF7-EA03-5EF4-8E1E-2E55DBF7B646","name":"ground cumin"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":2}},{"uuid":"6E4CE1C6-B620-51E3-87A5-08156BFBD621","order":4,"ingredient":{"uuid":"432C2858-27FF-5B98-9C4F-98377AEF62BA","name":"paprika"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":2}},{"uuid":"0F387D37-7614-53D2-878D-C58FA4009272","order":5,"ingredient":{"uuid":"BBF6786D-801A-58FB-B009-70D779E5E689","name":"lemon juice (for the turkey)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":3}},{"uuid":"9857F116-1C50-5B6B-8AD0-EC6320F918BF","order":6,"ingredient":{"uuid":"B9C2FB02-B63F-50EF-847E-0B822FA3E8B9","name":"jasmine rice (dry)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":3.25}},{"uuid":"A1A45B83-7060-5F5B-B0C1-CDDF0105F198","order":7,"ingredient":{"uuid":"F9D60E78-8AC4-5BC0-B331-8F52FC1C2BF9","name":"lemon juice (for the rice)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":4}},{"uuid":"37B93CAF-94F8-53CC-B6FB-1598F5E6B5D5","order":8,"ingredient":{"uuid":"AEB8C02D-CF1B-511F-9276-67AF628D0BB9","name":"dried dill or parsley"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":1}},{"uuid":"D067A127-1B02-56D3-8126-06B0D179B89E","order":9,"ingredient":{"uuid":"89803106-8986-5131-858F-7C9FD1D8EBD6","name":"zucchini (~1360 g, yields 825–975 g roasted)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"POUND","amount":3}},{"uuid":"869CBDC6-88BE-53B1-9619-0C53B80FCEB1","order":10,"ingredient":{"uuid":"D3ABF155-B7B1-5934-9169-BCFDE58494E2","name":"bell peppers (~340–620 g roasted; peppers vary hugely)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":6}},{"uuid":"7DECDB48-3968-5AA7-A1B6-150C5C7B1045","order":11,"ingredient":{"uuid":"E2B2312D-FDE5-5C3B-B53B-48B80DE59227","name":"red onions (~240–295 g roasted)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":3}},{"uuid":"88491930-E7CD-5413-9BBF-2BE744656F62","order":12,"ingredient":{"uuid":"C72CB03A-ABFA-5134-932D-B881188378DB","name":"Olive oil, salt, pepper"}},{"uuid":"8A9C4687-7BF8-58D1-BB89-F9D4FB2D471F","order":13,"ingredient":{"uuid":"21E97A2E-2E7D-55D9-9521-51EAC44EC71A","name":"Tzatziki, feta, cherry tomatoes, cucumber (added fresh when eating)"}}],"steps":[{"uuid":"72A30A38-5A63-5699-A40D-FF20193A50D3","order":0,"step":"Preheat the main oven to 425°F with the sheet pans inside. Hot pans sear on contact instead of steaming.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"344CF649-B745-5AB9-8155-25F3168630AE","order":1,"step":"Rinse 3 ¼ cups jasmine rice 2–3 times until the water runs mostly clear. Add to the Instant Pot with 3 ¼ cups water (1:1). Measure the water carefully — an over-filled pot gives waterlogged rice that packs soggy.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"C52DC849-52FC-5D65-B272-BEB165690B80","order":2,"step":"Confirm the valve is set to SEALING. Pressure Cook (Manual) on High for 3 minutes, natural release 10 minutes, then quick release. Start this first — it takes ~10 minutes to come to pressure.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"67C22C42-E27E-50C6-8242-2A03DCDCDF75","order":3,"step":"Cut the zucchini into thick ½-inch half-moons. Thin slices are mush by day 3.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"379EF5B8-52CE-5CFE-85D9-3976578DC9EB","order":4,"step":"Chop the 6 bell peppers and 3 red onions into pieces the same size as the zucchini so they roast evenly.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"706DEB69-DDE5-5A40-A663-461288C34158","order":5,"step":"Toss the vegetables with olive oil, salt, and pepper. Spread across 2 preheated pans in a single layer, nothing touching.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"4A4053D7-81BF-5970-A3B5-B32385C74375","order":6,"step":"Roast the vegetables at 425°F in the main oven for 20–25 minutes, flipping halfway. The edges should caramelize.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"87A66C35-01F5-5507-A03F-9006F2EBCFF6","order":7,"step":"Tip the roasted vegetables into a colander and let the standing water drain off. Zucchini gives up roughly 8% of its roasted weight as water, and anything not poured off here gets packed into the containers and makes them soggy by midweek.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"BCA3DEA2-D700-5342-88E7-3B0CF671E33F","order":8,"step":"Heat a large pan on the stovetop over medium-high. Add ~4.8 lbs ground turkey, breaking it up as it cooks. Brown 10–12 minutes until no pink remains and it reaches 165°F. Work in 2 batches if the pan is crowded — crowding steams the meat instead of browning it.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"0271E41F-E7BD-5499-936C-7DA8E2A8E056","order":9,"step":"Drain the excess liquid, then add the minced garlic, 2 tbsp oregano, 2 tsp cumin, 2 tsp paprika, salt, and pepper. Cook 2–3 minutes until fragrant.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"BA3B2AAB-282F-590A-B586-453FCF089C4F","order":10,"step":"Remove the turkey from the heat and stir in 3 tbsp lemon juice. The acid at the end is what makes it taste Mediterranean rather than generic.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"01539BD9-465C-5E3E-8467-56FF3EFA1A1C","order":11,"step":"Fluff the rice, then stir in 3–4 tbsp lemon juice, 1 tbsp dried dill or parsley, and salt. Add the lemon after cooking, not before.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"27E36702-02DD-534A-82C0-DC754B03BD22","order":12,"step":"Let the turkey, rice, and vegetables cool 10–15 minutes before portioning. Sealing hot food causes condensation and sogginess.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"E71AC371-1211-5BA8-98D1-DBBB87121536","order":13,"step":"Assembly line across 10 open containers: 155 g turkey, then 148 g rice, then 150 g roasted vegetables. No separate sauce container — the seasoning is already in the meat and the rice.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"6122C511-8CB1-5923-84FB-9A9AC2C3445F","order":14,"step":"Label with a dry-erase marker. 6 containers to the fridge, 4 to the freezer. Move freezer containers to the fridge the night before eating.","isSection":false}],"notes":"DIALED-IN — v3, last cooked 2026-08-31\n\nPER CONTAINER (10 total)\n  turkey: 155 g\n  rice: 148 g\n  veg: 150 g\n  total: 453 g\n\nSTORAGE: 6 fridge, 4 freezer\nFreezer containers move to the fridge the night before eating.\n\nFRESH TOPPINGS — NEVER PACKED: tzatziki, feta crumbles, cherry tomatoes, cucumber\nAdded at eating time only.\n\nTwo sessions behind these numbers, and they disagree more than anything else\nin the rotation:\n\n              undated log        2026-08-31\n  turkey      4.6 lb → 1500 g    4.8 lb → 1780 g   (0.719 vs 0.818)\n  zucchini    2.31 lb → 750 g    3.4 lb → 860 g    (0.716 vs 0.558, drained)\n  peppers     3 → 170 g          6 → 620 g         (57 vs 103 g each)\n  onions      3 → 240 g          3 → 295 g         (80 vs 98 g each)\n\n**The zucchini figures are not measured the same way.** The 2026-08-31 batch\ncame off the pan at 935 g and dropped to 860 g once the standing water was\npoured off — 75 g, about 8% of the roasted weight. Whether the earlier 750 g\nwas drained is unknown, so the two are not directly comparable and 0.558 is\nthe one to plan against, being both the lower and the better-defined.\n\nDraining is now step 8 and it matters beyond the yield. Water left on the\nvegetables gets packed into containers and is a large part of why zucchini\ngoes soft by midweek — the thick-cut rule exists for the same reason.\n\n**Peppers are the reason this recipe now calls for 6.** A pepper is not a unit\nof measurement — the two sessions differ by nearly 2× per pepper, a wider\nspread than broccoli crowns. Six covers the small end without overwhelming the\nbatch at the large end. Aldi does not let you weigh produce in store, so the\nweight range is here to plan against rather than to shop by.\n\n**Turkey at 0.818 is a light-drain number.** The prior session drained harder\nand got 0.719 on the same product. Plan at 0.72 and treat anything above as\nsurplus; planning high would leave you short. Watch whether the lighter drain\nmakes these containers greasier by day 4 — that is the tradeoff the taco bowls\nnotes warn about.\n\nThe 2026-08-31 rice is not recorded. 3 ½ cups came out at 1840 g, or 526 g per\ndry cup against 407–457 across three prior sessions — too much water in the\npot, not more rice. A measurement known to be contaminated is worse than none,\nbecause it looks exactly like signal, and averaging it in would have raised\nthe planning figure and under-bought rice on every recipe after it.\n\nPeppers hold up better than zucchini in the freezer. If you are freezing half\nthe batch, go lighter on zucchini and heavier on peppers in the freezer\ncontainers.\n\nThis is the no-chicken option in the rotation, and the only one with no\nbottled sauce anywhere in it — which is why the sodium projection is the\nlowest of the four.\n\nCold toppings — tzatziki, feta, cherry tomatoes, cucumber — go on fresh at\neating time, never packed. Aldi carries tzatziki and feta in the refrigerated\nsection.\n\nReheat, then top. A dollop of tzatziki and a handful of halved tomatoes takes\nthirty seconds and is the difference between a reheated bowl and something\nthat tastes made that day.","neutritionalInfo":"Serving Size: 1 container,\nCalories: 635 kcal,\nProtein: 49 g,\nCarbohydrates: 52 g,\nFat: 22 g,\nFiber: 5 g,\nSodium: 500 mg,\nSugar: 0 g","sourceName":"ten-containers","webLink":"https://zjbecker32.github.io/ten-containers/recipes/mediterranean-turkey-bowls/","tags":[],"images":[]}